*  mrbp_shallow_len — MINIMAL WIDENING WITNESS (s70, GOAL-RBP-EARN)
*
*  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the MATCH-RBP arm (s65e) qualifies on DEEP-ARRIVAL
*  graphs only.  Widening it to SHALLOW mains is blocked by DEPTH ACCOUNTING,
*  not by any register conflict (x86_fb_pinned() is 0 unconditionally, so rbp
*  is free of frame-base duty on every graph).  The hazard is precise:
*  a shallow main BAKES  off + op_zdepth  into every rsp-relative reader, so a
*  64-byte match frame that the planner does not see shifts every in-bracket
*  read that refers to a cell produced BEFORE the match.
*
*  N is produced into a spine cell BEFORE the match; LEN(*N) reads it from
*  INSIDE the bracket.  That is exactly the cross-frame read the widening must
*  not break.  Graph is deliberately defer-free/fence-free/arbno-free so it
*  lands in the shallow class (flat_deep_arrival = 0).
*
*  EXPECTED (SPITBOL oracle):   AB / CDEF / ok
*  USE: compare  SCRIP_MATCH_RBP=1  vs  =0  m3 AND m4 against x64/bin/sbl.
        N = 2
        S = 'ABCDEF'
        S ? LEN(*N) . FRONT REM . REST                  :F(BAD)
        OUTPUT = FRONT
        OUTPUT = REST
        OUTPUT = 'ok'                                   :(END0)
BAD     OUTPUT = 'BAD-match-failed'
END0
END
